Program          : DRVEC 0.12
Input Data File  : the .pre files
Output File      : rungs3.out
Model            : VARMA-VECM(2,0), M = 2 series, cointegration rank r = 0
Estimation       : Exact Unconditional Maximum Likelihood, Algorithm AS 311 (Mauricio 1997), xi sequence truncated at 1e-3
Transformation   : VECM to stationary VARMA (Mauricio 2006)
Deterministic    : case 3 -- E[nabla Y2] free, E[W] free
Structure        : F free, Theta absent (q = 0), Sigma free
Series           : muskrat mink   (2 in the nabla Y2 block, 0 in Y1)
Sample           : 61 observations from 1851, annual (raw 62)

=== The ladder: rungs at r = 0 ===

=== Entry gate: the factorisation contract ===

At r = 0 with diagonal Phi, Theta and Sigma the likelihood factorises,
so the joint fit must equal the sum of the univariate fits exactly.

  univariate 1 (p=2, q=0)   logL =     -24.0251813445
  univariate 2 (p=2, q=0)   logL =     -14.7874170655
                                 sum  =     -38.8125984100
                                 joint=     -38.8125984103
  (both sides untruncated; the fit's own logL, xi truncated at 1e-03, is -38.8125984103)

  crossing identity (joint - sum) = -2.477e-10   (tolerance 1.0e-06)   VERIFIED

  rung                          npar         logL         AIC         BIC
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  0  F, Theta, Sigma diagonal     5     -38.8126      1.4365      1.6095
  1  Sigma free                   6     -31.9991      1.2459      1.4535
  2  F and Theta free             8     -12.7876      0.6816      0.9584

  step        LR = 2*[L(k+1) - L(k)]    df    p-value
  -----------------------------------------------------
  0 -> 1          13.6270         1      0.0002
  1 -> 2          38.4231         2      0.0000

  These are ordinary nested comparisons: the restricted model is
  an INTERIOR point of the wider one, so the log-likelihood cannot
  fall and the statistic is chi2 on the stated degrees of freedom.
  The next rung -- adding the VEC matrix, r = 1 -- is not ordinary
  in either respect: the null sits ON the boundary of the alternative
  and B2 is unidentified under it.  It is reported by -lrtest, with
  a parametric bootstrap available for its distribution.
